<header><p class="enc-kicker">People / group</p><h1 class="enc-title">Krivichs</h1><p class="enc-meta">Also known as Krivichians, Krivichi</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">The Krivichians were an East Slavic tribal union of the early <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/middle-ages">Middle Ages</a>, living around the upper <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/dnieper">Dnieper</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/western-dvina">Western Dvina</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/volga">Volga</a>, with centres at <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/smolensk">Smolensk</a>, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/polotsk">Polotsk</a> and <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/izborsk">Izborsk</a>. According to the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/primary-chronicle">Primary Chronicle</a> they were among the tribes that invited the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/varangians">Varangians</a> to rule them in 862. From the late ninth century they paid tribute to the princes of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/kyiv">Kiev</a>, and their lands later formed the principalities of Polotsk and Smolensk.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/krivichs.jpg" alt="Krivichs" width="320" height="390" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: Koryakov Yuri · CC BY-SA 3.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Rus-10c-ethn.png" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
